<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Rich, 2nd Earl of Warwick</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1587">1587</a>–<a href="/years/1658">1658</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Rich, 2nd Earl of Warwick, was an English Puritan nobleman and colonial investor, a leading backer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/providence-island-company">Providence Island Company</a>, which settled Santa Catalina in 1630, and of other ventures in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-civil-war">English Civil War</a> he commanded the Parliamentarian navy and chaired the commission governing the colonies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-rich-2nd-earl-of-warwick.jpg" alt="Robert Rich, 2nd Earl of Warwick" width="320" height="534" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anthony van Dyck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Van_Dyck_-_Robert_Rich,_Second_Earl_of_Warwick,_1944.8.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
